-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/12"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_208_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "208", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/13"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_209_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "209", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/14"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_210_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "210", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/15"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_211_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "211", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/16"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD1", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "editorialPageNumber": "204", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26086/26086-0009.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> is at hand.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5291798731436036370\"><a href=\"#5291798731436036370\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans17\"><span id=\"documenttrans17\">17</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Zephaniah 1:7; Joel 1:15; and Isaiah 13:6.</p><hr></div></div></aside> Yea, prepare ye the way of the Lord, make strait his path.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8890871096748796541\"><a href=\"#8890871096748796541\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">In both the New Testament and the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a>, this phrase is attributed to John the Baptist. (Luke 3:4; Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=28\" class=\"externalLink\">22</a> [1 Nephi 10:7–10].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> Who will shrink because of offences, for offences must come, but woe to them by whom they come,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16317601215841413747\"><a href=\"#16317601215841413747\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans19\"><span id=\"documenttrans19\">19</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Luke 17:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> for the rock must fall on them and grind them to powder, for the fulness of the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"279505694414621642\"><a href=\"#279505694414621642\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6224\" topic=\"x6224\" title=\"Gentiles\">gentiles</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Gentiles\"><p>Those who were not members of the House of Israel. More specifically, members of the church identified gentiles as those whose lineage was not of the Jews or Lamanites (understood to be the American Indians in JS’s day). Certain prophecies indicated that ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/gentiles\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> is come in,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2541988666307675304\"><a href=\"#2541988666307675304\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans20\"><span id=\"documenttrans20\">20</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Romans 11:25.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and woe will be unto them if they do not repent and be <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1718839724489043398\"><a href=\"#1718839724489043398\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4058\" topic=\"x4058\" title=\"Baptism\">baptized</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Baptism\"><p>An ordinance in which an individual is immersed in water for the remission of sins. The Book of Mormon explained that those with necessary authority were to baptize individuals who had repented of their sins. Baptized individuals also received the gift of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/baptism\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> in the name of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ for the remission of their sins, and come in at the strait gate [p. 204]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> is at hand.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7422894171458209073\"><a href=\"#7422894171458209073\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans17\"><span id=\"documenttrans17\">17</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Zephaniah 1:7; Joel 1:15; and Isaiah 13:6.</p><hr></div></div></aside> Yea, prepare ye <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the way of the Lord, make strait <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>his path.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12497557009698076190\"><a href=\"#12497557009698076190\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">In both the New Testament and the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a>, this phrase is attributed to John the Baptist. (Luke 3:4; Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=28\" class=\"externalLink\">22</a> [1 Nephi 10:7–10].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> Who will shrink <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>because of offences, for offences <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>must come, but woe to them <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>by whom they come,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"815781443009784704\"><a href=\"#815781443009784704\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans19\"><span id=\"documenttrans19\">19</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Luke 17:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> for the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>rock must fall on them <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and grind them to powder, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>for the fulness of the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1937521287799852209\"><a href=\"#1937521287799852209\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6224\" topic=\"x6224\" title=\"Gentiles\">gentiles</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Gentiles\"><p>Those who were not members of the House of Israel. More specifically, members of the church identified gentiles as those whose lineage was not of the Jews or Lamanites (understood to be the American Indians in JS’s day). Certain prophecies indicated that ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/gentiles\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>is come in,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10178005875752898349\"><a href=\"#10178005875752898349\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans20\"><span id=\"documenttrans20\">20</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Romans 11:25.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and woe will <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>be unto them if they do not <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>repent and be <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14199891509160275794\"><a href=\"#14199891509160275794\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4058\" topic=\"x4058\" title=\"Baptism\">baptized</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Baptism\"><p>An ordinance in which an individual is immersed in water for the remission of sins. The Book of Mormon explained that those with necessary authority were to baptize individuals who had repented of their sins. Baptized individuals also received the gift of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/baptism\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>in the name of our Lord and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Savior Jesus Christ for the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>remission of their sins, and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>come in at the strait gate [p. 204]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_204_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_204_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_204.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_204_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/52/52_ppallen_204.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "52", "requestedPageNumber": "9", "numberOfPages": "16", "editorialT